9380bab390b3a6b8364bbe17" "q-109628/selection/95f14eebe13ee7d2ad352f26867e354291081c4d33359316bcd96ccbe273b634"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109628" :question/id #uuid "4a5c4536-304f-519c-bfd6-2a671aa1ec81" :question/math-academy-id "q-109628" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+3{t}^{1/2}{y}^{″}-7y=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-3{t}^{1/2}{y}^{″}+7y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-3{t}^{1/2}{x}_{3}+7{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=7{x}_{1}-3{t}^{1/2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=7{x}_{1}-3{t}^{1/2}{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109628/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82820104-bd75-549b-84e9-d225a7f4616b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109628"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583/selection/8dbce2c750cdd5eac7857a58d001fbee223d91d0de5b00e5d0f5a1f657c3a61f" :answer/id #uuid "d1f2bda3-822a-5085-bcb1-fe989d1af220" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{e}^{t}{x}_{1}+4t{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583/selection/e7a14e7a093cc020fdb5e14b8cc97b511cf623a1190414cf0601892b8276cb14" :answer/id #uuid "021b3d81-3569-588e-a3f0-e573183da9c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4t{x}_{1}+4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583/selection/e2335210cbdc1f46490e3c6cdf5054acaa4d8b75048c8d578d20f7ca6dca080b" :answer/id #uuid "11c50a90-5386-5dd2-999f-495fe88a92b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{t}{x}_{1}-4t{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583/selection/a37d8442252145baec92184bd4e58f6a5c31615fa1fb45a90dd6a3c987f8631a" :answer/id #uuid "d2b075cf-3d29-5cae-968b-6a8c8c052c9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4t{x}_{1}-4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583/selection/c8a0a32db53f4e645b498446916fe97f09c827035195e10b4d9402d495f9c72b" :answer/id #uuid "912e92de-64d4-5de5-8201-cd0aee021cc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{t}{x}_{1}+4t{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7c9c29c-cee1-5d71-8987-34ec050275c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109583/selection/e7a14e7a093cc020fdb5e14b8cc97b511cf623a1190414cf0601892b8276cb14" :answer-field/choices ["q-109583/selection/8dbce2c750cdd5eac7857a58d001fbee223d91d0de5b00e5d0f5a1f657c3a61f" "q-109583/selection/e7a14e7a093cc020fdb5e14b8cc97b511cf623a1190414cf0601892b8276cb14" "q-109583/selection/e2335210cbdc1f46490e3c6cdf5054acaa4d8b75048c8d578d20f7ca6dca080b" "q-109583/selection/a37d8442252145baec92184bd4e58f6a5c31615fa1fb45a90dd6a3c987f8631a" "q-109583/selection/c8a0a32db53f4e645b498446916fe97f09c827035195e10b4d9402d495f9c72b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109583" :question/id #uuid "1efb3be1-4590-5921-8a36-f0d39f3dba85" :question/math-academy-id "q-109583" :question/problem "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{e}^{t}{y}^{′}+4ty=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{e}^{t}{y}^{′}-4ty.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}-4t{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-4t{x}_{1}+4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=-4t{x}_{1}+4{e}^{t}{x}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109583/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82820104-bd75-549b-84e9-d225a7f4616b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623/selection/e5b84528aa87273728be982676388b70dd64f579dabf098aec7418f2cb48dded" :answer/id #uuid "cdb81b7a-5276-5f4f-b9cf-a2e70f17c14b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{3}{x}_{1}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{2}-2\\,{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623/selection/5dd2484a0c19ea6fd6c933eb9e55b1e62f63e4fe39e47b84d9c92cacb3acc217" :answer/id #uuid "d44693c0-8182-57b4-9e59-c3622ab5da71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-{t}^{3}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623/selection/9c7b7bf379baab1717d297738d55712bb714bbc0eb399ba16f1a80a864f871ba" :answer/id #uuid "85737b0d-4d60-5db4-8f82-d1cee0cf084a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}_{1}-{t}^{3}{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623/selection/9a2061207a2705bd3e9f895694fec8cf00de99f836fcedabf775f1975b4c690f" :answer/id #uuid "c56fcd49-7f91-5e0f-a992-a1b2dca68222" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{x}_{1}+{t}^{3}{x}_{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623/selection/d8134d0093a5f8633e49775c1566bf82d7c5a9f5672da02c80f8302426875223" :answer/id #uuid "bd576833-92a7-5105-bd30-98002bec0059" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+{t}^{3}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "934b1a8e-3165-5257-b908-7744e983e91d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109623/selection/9a2061207a2705bd3e9f895694fec8cf00de99f836fcedabf775f1975b4c690f" :answer-field/choices ["q-109623/selection/e5b84528aa87273728be982676388b70dd64f579dabf098aec7418f2cb48dded" "q-109623/selection/5dd2484a0c19ea6fd6c933eb9e55b1e62f63e4fe39e47b84d9c92cacb3acc217" "q-109623/selection/9c7b7bf379baab1717d297738d55712bb714bbc0eb399ba16f1a80a864f871ba" "q-109623/selection/9a2061207a2705bd3e9f895694fec8cf00de99f836fcedabf775f1975b4c690f" "q-109623/selection/d8134d0093a5f8633e49775c1566bf82d7c5a9f5672da02c80f8302426875223"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109623" :question/id #uuid "33461068-ee53-56f4-bf58-a85f4de3c6b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109623" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{y}^{″}-{t}^{3}{y}^{′}+2y=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{y}^{″}+{t}^{3}{y}^{′}-2y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+{t}^{3}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=-2{x}_{1}+{t}^{3}{x}_{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)=-2{x}_{1}+{t}^{3}{x}_{2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109623/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82820104-bd75-549b-84e9-d225a7f4616b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109623"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630/selection/83f54b0c6d4cb69347f538252e76e8c326cb3b29e6943e293a13a6e8289c8590" :answer/id #uuid "09e254ea-3081-5109-bf47-53e305d2f105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}{x}_{1}-{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630/selection/506bf8ab65bb83c6d42c21a033a32037827e70f9a9587c906911d44bc9e72e70" :answer/id #uuid "1bdf1b36-96bb-51b4-9e8b-e0129eb0162e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{t}{x}_{1}-{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{2}+t{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630/selection/60ee2f3e20a1297b8d2402acf6596237939b140b06ae4538b595225d14243ea1" :answer/id #uuid "3cb511c8-2490-553b-968e-e508805d810b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{2}-t{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630/selection/d6722c3e9c62d1af3200dc17b8759255b68d4d948524791283c282d041f54576" :answer/id #uuid "cb416fa1-288f-5267-b442-bf47af884c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{x}_{1}-{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{2}+{e}^{t}{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630/selection/943a382f4c4ed02bb6f199f31ab569ac04606307aa12d21fce67b3cac8fc18f0" :answer/id #uuid "7b52d687-6d33-5901-b0c9-0cb6ce148a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{1}-{e}^{t}{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a0fe0af-3fcb-59b1-b6c8-2707bd0394ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109630/selection/943a382f4c4ed02bb6f199f31ab569ac04606307aa12d21fce67b3cac8fc18f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-109630/selection/83f54b0c6d4cb69347f538252e76e8c326cb3b29e6943e293a13a6e8289c8590" "q-109630/selection/506bf8ab65bb83c6d42c21a033a32037827e70f9a9587c906911d44bc9e72e70" "q-109630/selection/60ee2f3e20a1297b8d2402acf6596237939b140b06ae4538b595225d14243ea1" "q-109630/selection/d6722c3e9c62d1af3200dc17b8759255b68d4d948524791283c282d041f54576" "q-109630/selection/943a382f4c4ed02bb6f199f31ab569ac04606307aa12d21fce67b3cac8fc18f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109630" :question/id #uuid "75dfee07-3584-54db-951a-175908c71eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-109630" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+{e}^{t}{y}^{″}-{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}y=0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-{e}^{t}{y}^{″}+{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-{e}^{t}{x}_{3}+{e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{1}-{e}^{t}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t)={e}^{\\sqrt{t}}{x}_{1}-{e}^{t}{x}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109630/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82820104-bd75-549b-84e9-d225a7f4616b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109630"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643/selection/f4cc812471fda7aa4c15381fdbade8d3e0bb49d0bfa6b30c084f90fb2c4e6741" :answer/id #uuid "4f29e7fd-7443-53e8-823a-6d9c057dc2c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8(6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643/selection/a51fb8193266e4eaed2c29f45281e4ac9ffce53e69e7f85d1ff74d5b04abcfa9" :answer/id #uuid "d07bfd76-df1b-5d78-abe7-4c787c512aae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643/selection/8987d0ad19dcb121d680f9867fc1f52cc28ae0bb3afc719a0932152e377d7678" :answer/id #uuid "3beeede1-a4ea-561f-93c6-f9f368428c41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4(6{x}_{2}-3\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643/selection/f5acba3cce3b182c410b8c4ab0b0da386cea1a537450e80e1cd47945138641c1" :answer/id #uuid "4b372f60-bd6c-5e27-9d7e-7a01f68b742b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643/selection/b778e7e34373a3b12ce5441ff219e9d5c1b4a56e0fc88d25e621ca6d51b70a74" :answer/id #uuid "d57f8041-d4a1-545e-a8b8-23250fe627b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18(2{x}_{2}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77a9d72e-88bb-5e94-9846-81022cf4dc22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109643/selection/b778e7e34373a3b12ce5441ff219e9d5c1b4a56e0fc88d25e621ca6d51b70a74" :answer-field/choices ["q-109643/selection/f4cc812471fda7aa4c15381fdbade8d3e0bb49d0bfa6b30c084f90fb2c4e6741" "q-109643/selection/a51fb8193266e4eaed2c29f45281e4ac9ffce53e69e7f85d1ff74d5b04abcfa9" "q-109643/selection/8987d0ad19dcb121d680f9867fc1f52cc28ae0bb3afc719a0932152e377d7678" "q-109643/selection/f5acba3cce3b182c410b8c4ab0b0da386cea1a537450e80e1cd47945138641c1" "q-109643/selection/b778e7e34373a3b12ce5441ff219e9d5c1b4a56e0fc88d25e621ca6d51b70a74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109643" :question/id #uuid "53f5f48b-e375-5e2f-99ed-48004360183f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109643" :question/problem "The third-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-6\\sqrt{t}\\,{y}^{″}+12{y}^{′}=0,\\,y(1)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2,\\,{y}^{″}(1)=-3\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=q \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{3}(1)=r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t),$ and $p,$ $q$ and $r$ are constants. Calculate  $(p+q-r)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={x}_{1}(1)=-2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(1) & ={x}_{2}(1)=2 \\\\ {y}^{″}(1) & ={x}_{3}(1)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=6\\sqrt{t}\\,{y}^{″}-12{y}^{′}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}-12{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=2 \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=-12{x}_{2}+6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{3}(1)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=-2,q=2,r=-3,f(t)=-12{x}_{2}+6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p+q-r)\\cdot f(t) & =(-2+2-(-3))(-12{x}_{2}+6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(-2+2+3)(-12{x}_{2}+6\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =3(-6)(2{x}_{2}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-18(2{x}_{2}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638/selection/4def7799a747191059548f13c2687348b09bcb824fade956d48b265251ae48b5" :answer/id #uuid "67842a88-c857-5310-b921-0889037ea3a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638/selection/3de644339c28cb4bd7cff4f2ecf1bd6b86f972f81bedec2b01267404e1f2894b" :answer/id #uuid "c6f49976-b5e6-5ceb-b6a6-d1a50892cc22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638/selection/11068ebb40320d1f09190ba37667a7227c39def7a8e685e5399b3bbc862a2d25" :answer/id #uuid "97fabf27-aab3-5983-bb6b-3f3a75309842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(4{x}_{1}-t{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638/selection/2d84e31bde293cb9e3cbc43dbcc1c08d2180a95611f71a7d1a89ff8587466cf3" :answer/id #uuid "91cd9371-5de8-5c5a-8ada-db21a7d50993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-t{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638/selection/1e6e4246f646c807f6060ac5a4a0741ce099032f32daf621e817c3c71d16399a" :answer/id #uuid "27181915-31b3-5850-95e5-7f1611824014" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2(4{x}_{1}-t{x}_{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "55f70100-3dee-5d38-8467-138a8312efae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109638/selection/3de644339c28cb4bd7cff4f2ecf1bd6b86f972f81bedec2b01267404e1f2894b" :answer-field/choices ["q-109638/selection/4def7799a747191059548f13c2687348b09bcb824fade956d48b265251ae48b5" "q-109638/selection/3de644339c28cb4bd7cff4f2ecf1bd6b86f972f81bedec2b01267404e1f2894b" "q-109638/selection/11068ebb40320d1f09190ba37667a7227c39def7a8e685e5399b3bbc862a2d25" "q-109638/selection/2d84e31bde293cb9e3cbc43dbcc1c08d2180a95611f71a7d1a89ff8587466cf3" "q-109638/selection/1e6e4246f646c807f6060ac5a4a0741ce099032f32daf621e817c3c71d16399a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109638" :question/id #uuid "c7a70976-fd43-5b84-a619-3ddab5c39c5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-109638" :question/problem "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}-ty=0,\\,y(2)=-2,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=-3\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(2)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(2)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & ={x}_{1}(2)=-2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(2) & ={x}_{2}(2)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=-4{y}^{′}+ty.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=-4{x}_{2}+t{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(2)=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{2}(2)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=-2,q=-3,f(t)=t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q)\\cdot f(t) & =(-2-(-3))(t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =(1)(t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =t{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109638/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642/selection/7a6101acb8fb5c3e76af5f6ac266687042e5de511f4328faead90e4bf9cc22eb" :answer/id #uuid "f989cdf3-7473-5902-bf7e-53360b092941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15{x}_{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642/selection/b4aefd2f52f895e1a81f285d397d8de56d7b2b764d5c2016b4f30e3e789d4e41" :answer/id #uuid "5b7714ec-4823-564d-8635-fde5f41e3cfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12{x}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642/selection/6cb259ffc66313c5c52f35d88f2c0c10dd92185efe21493ac75b949c3faa5027" :answer/id #uuid "9c9ea6cc-893e-5545-a4f4-83353395b4cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642/selection/9b5755b05027a7738b58983fbddec931126955cebe27b83c75171a6f5f3b551c" :answer/id #uuid "eb6ef9a7-0537-536c-86a8-a403320e72a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21{x}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642/selection/ca9058cfa8f9a0e73c7b5723f67e22353957062f43a9db7c36a46d0b5706c304" :answer/id #uuid "064eef02-ab1f-5141-98f7-d23c632da105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9{x}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f01c3cb2-69d4-5a1d-9b22-269fa2b92125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109642/selection/6cb259ffc66313c5c52f35d88f2c0c10dd92185efe21493ac75b949c3faa5027" :answer-field/choices ["q-109642/selection/7a6101acb8fb5c3e76af5f6ac266687042e5de511f4328faead90e4bf9cc22eb" "q-109642/selection/b4aefd2f52f895e1a81f285d397d8de56d7b2b764d5c2016b4f30e3e789d4e41" "q-109642/selection/6cb259ffc66313c5c52f35d88f2c0c10dd92185efe21493ac75b949c3faa5027" "q-109642/selection/9b5755b05027a7738b58983fbddec931126955cebe27b83c75171a6f5f3b551c" "q-109642/selection/ca9058cfa8f9a0e73c7b5723f67e22353957062f43a9db7c36a46d0b5706c304"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109642" :question/id #uuid "c382da1a-1bd0-5d53-b506-6fe5031cfb29" :question/math-academy-id "q-109642" :question/problem "The third-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+3{y}^{′}=0,\\,y(2)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=1,\\,{y}^{″}(2)=2\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(2)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(2)=q \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{3}(2)=r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t),$ and $p,$ $q$ and $r$ are constants. Calculate $(p+q-r)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & ={x}_{1}(2)=-1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(2) & ={x}_{2}(2)=1 \\\\ {y}^{″}(2) & ={x}_{3}(2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-3{y}^{′}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-3{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(2)=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(2)=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=-3{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{3}(2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=-1,q=1,r=2,f(t)=-3{x}_{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p+q-r)\\cdot f(t) & =(-1+1-2)(-3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =(-2)(-3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =6{x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-107906"] :question/problem "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-3{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=3\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={x}_{1}(1)=2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(1) & ={x}_{2}(1)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=3{y}^{′}-2y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=2,q=3,f(t)=-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q)\\cdot f(t) & =(2-3)f(t) \\\\  & =-f(t) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641/selection/6998de77f1b8263b4aaf796c48532a17e44643c2147536b25d9b881c8c413e98" :answer/id #uuid "58841aa9-ecd9-58fe-b8f3-1ef30f299dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(-3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+12{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641/selection/3d03be51356dfdabc1a73637879ef9a1953ae286a2bf194ed954bed20fb53883" :answer/id #uuid "3cd7130b-2cff-501f-acd4-54f12cd300fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}-12{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641/selection/333182ed3144f890d887c0c411ee4d1a700f339623cd93aea4a7508885ee4c2d" :answer/id #uuid "ecf758bb-930c-5989-a8dd-fac3f629bb5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(12{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641/selection/0310c9728448d22009557eff2928f46e6ce33e460245d0c74000400b9f144291" :answer/id #uuid "8d5b9e2b-6059-5789-bb8f-04297f72632e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(12{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641/selection/4a00f2cd6e28e3c549100606754ec7d5d619496c76da2c165c54a22964decd0e" :answer/id #uuid "25e6dad9-df83-5646-b630-1545316ac404" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(-12{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd2f899e-a53c-52a5-af8f-ea505b5e2066" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109641/selection/0310c9728448d22009557eff2928f46e6ce33e460245d0c74000400b9f144291" :answer-field/choices ["q-109641/selection/6998de77f1b8263b4aaf796c48532a17e44643c2147536b25d9b881c8c413e98" "q-109641/selection/3d03be51356dfdabc1a73637879ef9a1953ae286a2bf194ed954bed20fb53883" "q-109641/selection/333182ed3144f890d887c0c411ee4d1a700f339623cd93aea4a7508885ee4c2d" "q-109641/selection/0310c9728448d22009557eff2928f46e6ce33e460245d0c74000400b9f144291" "q-109641/selection/4a00f2cd6e28e3c549100606754ec7d5d619496c76da2c165c54a22964decd0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109641" :question/id #uuid "250135ef-e54c-5b53-9ec4-19d900601af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109641" :question/problem "The third-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+3{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}-12y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1,\\,{y}^{″}(0)=3\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=q \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{3}(0)=r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t),$ and $p,$ $q$ and $r$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q+r)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={x}_{1}(0)=2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(0) & ={x}_{2}(0)=1 \\\\ {y}^{″}(0) & ={x}_{3}(0)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-3{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+12y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-3{x}_{3}+4{x}_{2}+12{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=12{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3},\\, & {x}_{3}(0)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=2,q=1,r=3,f(t)=12{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3},$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q+r)\\cdot f(t) & =(2-1+3)(12{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(12{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109641/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c19ef7ec-19a3-533a-bcd9-1b775f301801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109641"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692/selection/96afba7ebf18a2f78aa346b6be67460136de8b2c65c7d3aa01ef5de6c748c6c0" :answer/id #uuid "886cb56a-fb01-5225-acd8-211db5b29c46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{3} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692/selection/2aa3a05249061a2eb60ca40cf6eb80802e68dfd81ca51419cc8c591de5f6282d" :answer/id #uuid "ae43508a-6545-5ea9-ab3f-36babccbdb36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692/selection/93367425f08a53f2ce3aca88ed5cee68a948730835f62e2c4893a6c8eea8f342" :answer/id #uuid "43e01697-c1d7-500d-8b9c-7db3788b5dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{3} & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692/selection/ae0fc992d477c3e5c48234bdcd63562b6b4de172eb928662295b074455254264" :answer/id #uuid "278b9b9a-dddd-5b5e-aa90-4a09860dbb68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692/selection/236f17673b932850f69f5792f74427345b5156ba135e0f1fdd375572ff560242" :answer/id #uuid "28465812-4bdb-56d6-b1a8-f14ed5d801a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "68c0d915-ab28-5b50-9db8-d473be3d03d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109692/selection/2aa3a05249061a2eb60ca40cf6eb80802e68dfd81ca51419cc8c591de5f6282d" :answer-field/choices ["q-109692/selection/96afba7ebf18a2f78aa346b6be67460136de8b2c65c7d3aa01ef5de6c748c6c0" "q-109692/selection/2aa3a05249061a2eb60ca40cf6eb80802e68dfd81ca51419cc8c591de5f6282d" "q-109692/selection/93367425f08a53f2ce3aca88ed5cee68a948730835f62e2c4893a6c8eea8f342" "q-109692/selection/ae0fc992d477c3e5c48234bdcd63562b6b4de172eb928662295b074455254264" "q-109692/selection/236f17673b932850f69f5792f74427345b5156ba135e0f1fdd375572ff560242"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109692" :question/id #uuid "c0e82d28-4193-5245-8695-f97b44951b09" :question/math-academy-id "q-109692" :question/problem "The second-order differential equation $3{y}^{″}+9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{y}^{′}+y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\\,y(t)={x}_{1}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{y}^{′}-\\frac{1}{3}y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{1}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109692/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7657ff9-3918-5080-b9a2-8f6a6d8b4fd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109692"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695/selection/8a236e501d52126cb889385f0d30f7b4cbfdb66163cbe8f1955e21cb3c620bed" :answer/id #uuid "4597d81d-9c57-5508-820e-c001533c89a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-(3{t}^{2}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695/selection/d5ee214fc4ebdb964d67239e3da5811b7c787bb4ef47ec0ccbaa764f05d5fe99" :answer/id #uuid "fd789455-28ee-5696-b105-c4946a505917" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695/selection/7697b742b99d3fcc3812743ec3e07f8fd8e673d6fe459880d276020f3ffa1217" :answer/id #uuid "ce8c5384-ddee-5573-9d7e-067e5948d126" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695/selection/9909387cad715efd84810cbc3093a5f44d425ad2b050b39fa080445b6dbde394" :answer/id #uuid "027cf64a-6ec3-580b-a9c6-6b9f3a0d6e6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695/selection/7a14e161b9701c2c1678a00df7b4ce39522df64ffff663ec5c1c7f84264bf6b6" :answer/id #uuid "cb2f1240-9dfe-5491-bb44-93852b6b634f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{t}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3bdcc9-f3c5-5474-958a-5362aa3718eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109695/selection/7697b742b99d3fcc3812743ec3e07f8fd8e673d6fe459880d276020f3ffa1217" :answer-field/choices ["q-109695/selection/8a236e501d52126cb889385f0d30f7b4cbfdb66163cbe8f1955e21cb3c620bed" "q-109695/selection/d5ee214fc4ebdb964d67239e3da5811b7c787bb4ef47ec0ccbaa764f05d5fe99" "q-109695/selection/7697b742b99d3fcc3812743ec3e07f8fd8e673d6fe459880d276020f3ffa1217" "q-109695/selection/9909387cad715efd84810cbc3093a5f44d425ad2b050b39fa080445b6dbde394" "q-109695/selection/7a14e161b9701c2c1678a00df7b4ce39522df64ffff663ec5c1c7f84264bf6b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109695" :question/id #uuid "0737f5ff-3d66-5f51-b7b8-b8bf8fe97f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-109695" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}+5{y}^{″}-3{t}^{2}{y}^{′}=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & a & c\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-5{y}^{″}+3{t}^{2}{y}^{′}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=-5{x}_{3}+3{t}^{2}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=3{t}^{2}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3{t}^{2} & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $a=3{t}^{2},b=1,c=-5,$ and $a+b+c=3{t}^{2}-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109695/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7657ff9-3918-5080-b9a2-8f6a6d8b4fd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "33931923-d925-577d-8770-bef2a1650629" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "17049e80-8f02-5d15-8fc8-7277e3f1915b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "444d6424-0929-520f-899b-be78dcc9ae4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "1dbb47cd-2316-5f76-a401-54289ce15a8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "7af81163-828b-573b-9354-788acd2fdccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c0b23f-a466-51e2-ab19-c42f45659baa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109698/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer-field/choices ["q-109698/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-109698/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" "q-109698/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-109698/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-109698/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109698" :question/id #uuid "df09efa8-0851-5057-97e5-5c263f3619c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-109698" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}-2{y}^{″}+13{y}^{′}=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & b & c\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=2{y}^{″}-13{y}^{′}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=2{x}_{3}-13{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=-13{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -13 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $a=1,b=-13,c=2,$ and $a+b+c=-10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109698/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7657ff9-3918-5080-b9a2-8f6a6d8b4fd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109698"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "4df3f7cb-645a-57bf-ab31-18fb013189b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "a0dd2f67-b61f-5d54-a262-2e1a780f0d39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "86287066-75f9-5b18-a5af-c42b6647e606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8691544e-d94b-55df-9c58-7b5a0ee99681" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "caf0f5a2-c0e1-53ef-8f3f-63dd76973658" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dce21225-5b3e-5167-97af-ca985147f3ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109696/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-109696/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-109696/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-109696/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-109696/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-109696/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109696" :question/id #uuid "854fff95-597d-57db-aef7-0e595418f814" :question/math-academy-id "q-109696" :question/problem "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}-3{y}^{′}+4y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ a & c & 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=3{y}^{′}-4y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=3{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=-4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $a=-4,b=1,c=3,$ and $a+b+c=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109696/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7657ff9-3918-5080-b9a2-8f6a6d8b4fd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109696"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646/selection/3b9afb65baa5f4fe1c75b621ee7857df6142fce4e94d2d9db3d1791512cd99fd" :answer/id #uuid "20740ef5-cb16-5776-8c6b-0fe3ef7e8a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646/selection/3e6e88cd348d969334b3e35b31fe6c68a2891bc23051d17a2e198a205349c411" :answer/id #uuid "786bd0e1-3964-5b58-b0f2-c86469191f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646/selection/eebb768f0fccf5dad06f8b5e8cd4d510ee2569adc32d6a55360295b4e6ae6d64" :answer/id #uuid "a18b2a01-5e4c-58e2-9412-5463c0dbbcad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646/selection/fc57dc1e5a920b87e1bef94f6e47531f7aeebf0ff90a814ee76558caa7f44cb1" :answer/id #uuid "738e0830-d962-576d-834e-20d66227135a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646/selection/ef0cc803b5852b5bfb99533d5ae5347bfc2e75551d43180e5e88bfe2e33ef84d" :answer/id #uuid "379e21da-82bd-5cbf-b974-6f7040f62156" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d81be2-b251-5020-9de9-afbdb44ce8f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109646/selection/eebb768f0fccf5dad06f8b5e8cd4d510ee2569adc32d6a55360295b4e6ae6d64" :answer-field/choices ["q-109646/selection/3b9afb65baa5f4fe1c75b621ee7857df6142fce4e94d2d9db3d1791512cd99fd" "q-109646/selection/3e6e88cd348d969334b3e35b31fe6c68a2891bc23051d17a2e198a205349c411" "q-109646/selection/eebb768f0fccf5dad06f8b5e8cd4d510ee2569adc32d6a55360295b4e6ae6d64" "q-109646/selection/fc57dc1e5a920b87e1bef94f6e47531f7aeebf0ff90a814ee76558caa7f44cb1" "q-109646/selection/ef0cc803b5852b5bfb99533d5ae5347bfc2e75551d43180e5e88bfe2e33ef84d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109646" :question/id #uuid "e7713dc2-84ca-5bb4-a57a-9ba6579282a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-109646" :question/problem "The second-order differential equation ${y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+3y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\\,y(t)={x}_{1}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{y}^{′}-3y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence, $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109646/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7657ff9-3918-5080-b9a2-8f6a6d8b4fd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9040"] :question/problem "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\ny''' - 3\\sqrt{t}\\, y'' + t^3 y' - 4t^2 y= 0\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1(t) = y(t),$ $x_2(t) = y'(t)$ and $x_3(t) = y''(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of $x_1, x_2,$ and $x_3.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $(y'''),$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny''' = 3\\sqrt{t}\\,y'' - t^3 y' + 4t^2 y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\ny''' = 3\\sqrt{t}\\, x_3 - t^3 x_2 + 4t^2 x_1.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=4{t}^{2}\\,{x}_{1}-{t}^{3}{x}_{2}+3\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $f(t) = 4t^2 x_1 - t^3 x_2 + 3\\sqrt{t} \\,x_3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9041"] :question/problem "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\ny''  + y' - 6y= 0 , \\quad y(0)= 1, \\quad y'(0)= 4\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1(t) = y(t),$ $x_2(t) = y'(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also convert the initial conditions, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & ={x}_{1}(0)=1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(0) & ={x}_{2}(0)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of $x_1$ and $x_2.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $(y''),$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny'' = - y' + 6y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\ny'' = - x_2 + 6x_1.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=6{x}_{1}-{x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=1, q=4, f(t) = 6x_1 - x_2,$ and \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(p-q)\\cdot f(t) & =(1-4)(6{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =-3(6{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9138"] :question/problem "The second-order differential equation $y'' + 5y' - 2y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ where \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070402/assets/59e386be8b30fca475a2e0d164687a6561b9ab368b9879fc301d328896d184fd.png)\nFind the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′} & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of $x_1$ and $x_2.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $(y''),$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny''= -5y' + 2y.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\ny'' = -5x_2 + 2x_1.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf x'(t) = A\\mathbf x(t)$ as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070402/assets/f35de5e6f066144c4130e38304abbff552730dc1fe97828572a66e68970c5d52.png)\n\nHence, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070402/assets/314f9dcf277b61dac9985c448aed98113516592e3822cc47a8566d28a480651b.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
